  "body": "## Result and scope\n\nAll **3600 ordered whole-hyperplane rectangles** on the fixed60 Gaussian E8 lines are allowed, including the2640 nonorthogonal-normal types excluded by PR767. If the **fitted binary matrix B is symmetric**, any finite scalar binary decomposition pays at least **180 Gaussian pairing-rank units /360 rational units**. Individual totals may be asymmetric and arbitrary repetitions are allowed. A fitting B with just one asymmetric unordered pair still costs at least66 Gaussian units.\n\nThe structural proof is invertible characteristic-two congruence: O is the symmetric rank60 hyperplane incidence with O1=1; Q=O^-1; X=QBQ^T. Symmetric B gives diag(X)=Q diag(B)=1, forcing all60 rank3 diagonal types. The conditional fully favorable Dfc budgets are -120-240s and -120-12s, respectively, so these classes cannot give positive saving even with every additional expense granted free. **No new supplier or kappa; no sharpness at180 or unrestricted cost lower bound is claimed.**\n\nFor arbitrary fitted B, the new defect formula is diag(X)=1 XOR sum_e (B_ij XOR B_ji)(Q_i AND Q_j), over450 unordered orthogonal edges. Its exact image has rank59 and consists of **all even-weight vectors**. A genuine34-edge nonsymmetric fitting witness has no diagonal types and bill4736, showing why the forced-diagonal implication cannot be extended to all completions. It is a scope-boundary control, not a cheap construction.\n\n## Evidence and reproduction\n\nAdds only research/gaussian-hyperplane-allpairs/: README proof, complete SELECTION, TASK, source pins, registered VERIFY, exact RESULT and standard-library verifier. Checks cover3600 physical pairing ranks,900 directed fitting generators,62 separately realified rational ranks, complete diagonal-image basis, literal rectangle replay, and11 semantic controls. Checks remain active under -O.\n\n```sh\nuv run --python 3.12 --no-project python -I -O -B research/gaussian-hyperplane-allpairs/verify.py\nuv run --python 3.12 --no-project python scripts/research_package.py --package research/gaussian-hyperplane-allpairs\n```\n\nObserved locally on macOS arm64 / CPython3.12.12: optimized --write smoke PASS and registered replay PASS, with pairs=3600 symmetric_floor=180 single_asymmetry_floor=66 diagonal_image_rank=59 zero_diagonal_bill=4736 controls=11 no_new_kappa. The parent independently reviewed the proof and replayed the registered package before granting publication. No GitHub CI, Lean/kernel run, selected cold replay or full repository suite is claimed.\n\n## Assignment, overlap, and credit\n\nIndependent seed **ab997fb2d6ec74f382d67332d715ef38**, complex-mechanisms / complex-rank-shape-decoder; exact base e112d71c8d7bb32435debcc54df932593dd8223a. Explicit bounded pivot: unrestricted allpairs bill optimization remained unresolved; the deliverable is the reciprocity obstruction and complete unrestricted diagonal-image classification, not a successful physical supplier. Original complete5%-ceiling acceptance gate is neither weakened nor claimed passed.\n\nClaim and pivot: #research-claim-and-completion-record . Shared complete329openPR/692discussion snapshot plus targeted live/local/merged checks are recorded. PR767 restricts normal pairs without requiring B symmetry; this package changes that hypothesis rather than resubmitting its960-type theorem. PR770/868 concern clique-certificate limits; recent PR2017 concerns Eisenstein good reduction, not Gaussian60 reciprocity.\n\nCredit Charles Bethin/cbethin PR767 at96b4b74677d1bef99e8346bfb6a4ed0531e58a62 for exact geometry and the restricted predecessor; Joel Pulikkan/GamingPuzzled PR620 for the Gaussian model; Sagar Thakrar/thakrarsagar PR738 for the distinct unrestricted floor40; Douglas R. Colkitt/Mister-Meeseeks for related planning/Hurwitz precedent; DreamingOfClouds for inherited format accounting. Frozen sources and selected frontier remain unchanged.\n\nPrepared for Adam Gall with substantial OpenAI Codex GPT-6 Astra assistance. Apache-2.0; no independent human or formal-kernel review claimed.\n\n## Research claim and completion record\n\nStatus: completed. The claim record is preserved here so this PR is self-contained. Historical coordination links in the committed research metadata refer to this record; the separate coordination discussion is being removed.\n\nDONE \u2014 independent seed ab997fb2d6ec74f382d67332d715ef38, complex-rank-shape-decoder. PR https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2066 ; full commit4af8904d4a5aade6d53a823c6cae73cdfe5a6562, from base e112d71c8d7bb32435debcc54df932593dd8223a. Package research/gaussian-hyperplane-allpairs.\n\nAll3600 whole Gaussian E8 hyperplane rectangle types: symmetric FITTED B forces all60 rank3 diagonal types, hence Gaussian cost>=180; individual totals may be asymmetric and repeated. One asymmetric unordered pair still costs>=66. Complete favorable Dfc deficits are <=-120-240s / -120-12s, so these classes cannot give positive saving. Arbitrary-asymmetry coefficient diagonal image is exactly the even-weight59-dimensional subspace; a genuine34-edge nonsymmetric fitting control has zero diagonal types and bill4736. No sharp180 attainment, unrestricted optimum, physical supplier, kappa or CI claim.\n\nExplicit bounded pivot retained: unrestricted allpairs bill optimization was not solved; final deliverable is the reciprocity obstruction plus exact unrestricted diagonal-image classification. This replaces PR767 normal-pair restriction by global fitted-matrix reciprocity, not a resubmission of its960-type theorem. Source credit includes Charles Bethin/PR767, Joel Pulikkan/PR620, Sagar Thakrar/PR738, Douglas R. Colkitt and DreamingOfClouds.\n\nOptimized smoke and registered CPython3.12.12 replay passed:3600pairing ranks,900directed generators,62independent realifications, rank59image,11semantic controls. Parent separately reviewed/replayed and granted publication. Reproduce: uv run --python 3.12 --no-project python scripts/research_package.py --package research/gaussian-hyperplane-allpairs . Final targeted live/local/merged overlap checks recorded; selected frontier and predecessor bytes unchanged. Claim complete/released. Substantial OpenAI Codex GPT-6 Astra assistance; Apache-2.0.\n",
